econd equation it is $4$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-20$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $20$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&20u + 9v = 7 \\\\ &(4u - 8v = -12)\\cdot (-5)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20u + 9v &= 7 \\\\\n-20u + 40v &= 60 \\\\\n(9v + 40v) &= (7 + 60) \\\\\n49v &= 67\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39984c68-52c5-5346-96ed-793bff46e6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509150} {:answer/id #uuid "4713ec37-422e-594c-819d-cacd1edf2a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4713ec37-422e-594c-819d-cacd1edf2a8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509155} :answer-field/id #uuid "751b0f60-f8d4-5160-8cc1-482c0b17d4f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c0c0b8-da16-